                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238867382",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198163557301",
                            "num_reviews": 51,
                            "playtime_forever": 1426,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 18,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1426,
                            "last_played": 1793307382
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a short (About 30 minute), recycled arcade-style game from the late 1990s with updated (by 2010 standards) 3D graphics from the original 2D sprites. The majority of the content is from an overarching narrative of this game, RefleX and Kamui with difficulty settings and an in-depth scoring system.\r\n\r\n-Scoring system comes down to building a multiplier with certain weapons and then capitalizing on it through high-scoring weapons. It's not just a clever incentive for re-playability, it aides you in the completion of the short, but very difficult campaign by increasing your 1UPs, granting you more opportunities to progress if you get stuck, which you most definitely will even if you're a hardcore shmup fan.\r\n\r\nI mainly played this on the Anbernic Win600 handheld, treating it like a portable experience is the best way to play this, but absolutely worth giving a shot even if you just have a dedicated PC",
